and working with a trainer,
but, I don't know --

00:11:05.764 --> 00:11:08.200
something about them
seems a little off.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:10.302
[ Laughter ]

00:11:10.302 --> 00:11:12.771
Officials have announced
that a nearly 1/4-mile-long

00:11:12.771 --> 00:11:14.440
container ship
that has been stuck

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:17.208
in the Suez Canal, in Egypt,
since Tuesday

00:11:17.208 --> 00:11:18.810
could take weeks to free.

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:21.246
Even worse, it's carrying
that thing you rush-ordered

00:11:21.246 --> 00:11:23.716
for your wife's birthday.

00:11:23.716 --> 00:11:26.084
A Spirit Airlines flight
was diverted to Denver yesterday

00:11:26.084 --> 00:11:27.652
after a passenger
allegedly tried

00:11:27.652 --> 00:11:29.721
to open an emergency exit door.

00:11:29.721 --> 00:11:31.357
Luckily, it was a Spirit plane,

00:11:31.357 --> 00:11:33.759
so the emergency exit
was just painted on.

00:11:33.759 --> 00:11:35.494
[ Laughter ]

00:11:35.494 --> 00:11:39.298
The Olympic torch relay began
today in Fukushima, Japan,

00:11:39.298 --> 00:11:40.665
and will be carried
around the country

00:11:40.665 --> 00:11:41.934
by more than 10,000 people

00:11:41.934 --> 00:11:44.603
before arriving
in Tokyo's Olympic Stadium.

00:11:44.603 --> 00:11:47.406
That story again --
an open flame will be run

00:11:47.406 --> 00:11:49.675
through a nuclear fallout
disaster area

00:11:49.675 --> 00:11:52.344
before being passed
person-to-person 10,000 times

00:11:52.344 --> 00:11:53.712
during a contagious pandemic.

00:11:53.712 --> 00:11:55.114
Let the games begin!

00:11:55.114 --> 00:11:56.181
[ Laughter ]

00:11:56.181 --> 00:11:58.717
Officials in China
recently closed

00:11:58.717 --> 00:12:01.286
the country's
first sex doll hotel

00:12:01.286 --> 00:12:04.390
and released a statement
attributing the move to reasons

00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:07.559
"not convenient to explain."

00:12:07.559 --> 00:12:10.296
And I think I speak
for everyone when I say,

00:12:10.296 --> 00:12:11.864
"I'll, uh --

00:12:11.864 --> 00:12:13.165
I'll make time for this one."

00:12:13.165 --> 00:12:15.501
[ Laughter ]

00:12:15.501 --> 00:12:16.702
Also, what do you mean,

00:12:16.702 --> 00:12:19.438
the reasons are
"not convenient to explain"?

00:12:19.438 --> 00:12:22.074
I think it's pretty easy
to explain.

00:12:22.074 --> 00:12:25.977
"Sex doll hotel"
is the explanation.

00:12:25.977 --> 00:12:29.281
I don't even like to touch the
remote control in a hotel room.

00:12:29.281 --> 00:12:30.615
I'm joking.
They actually closed it

00:12:30.615 --> 00:12:31.917
because, against all odds,

00:12:31.917 --> 00:12:32.985
nobody came.

00:12:32.985 --> 00:12:39.959
[ Laughter ]

00:12:39.959 --> 00:12:41.193
[ Sighs ]

00:12:41.193 --> 00:12:42.595
[ Laughter ]

00:12:42.595 --> 00:12:45.063
Organizers of the annual
Hash Bash marijuana rally

00:12:45.063 --> 00:12:46.899
in Ann Arbor, Michigan,
announced on Tuesday

00:12:46.899 --> 00:12:49.568
that the event will be held
virtually this year.

00:12:49.568 --> 00:12:52.237
Which is risky, because,
once everyone realizes

00:12:52.237 --> 00:12:54.906
they can do it from their couch,
they'll never go back.

00:12:54.906 --> 00:12:56.909
[ Laughter ]
And finally, today was --

00:12:56.909 --> 00:12:59.078
Ooh, actually, uh,
before I tell this joke --

00:12:59.078 --> 00:13:02.514
There's a lot of national days
on the calendar.

00:13:02.514 --> 00:13:05.517
Pretty much every day,
in the setups of our jokes,

00:13:05.517 --> 00:13:07.386
you find out
what national day it is.

00:13:07.386 --> 00:13:09.855
And something that's never been
attempted before

00:13:09.855 --> 00:13:11.190
has happened this week.

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:13.258
Mike Scollins,
a writer for the show,

00:13:13.258 --> 00:13:16.094
has told a "Today was
National Whatever Day"

00:13:16.094 --> 00:13:18.797
with a punch line
three days in a row,

00:13:18.797 --> 00:13:21.099
which is known as a turkey.

00:13:21.099 --> 00:13:23.301
No one's ever done four
in a row,

00:13:23.301 --> 00:13:25.003
but he's about to try.

00:13:25.003 --> 00:13:28.707
And we're about to see if he
can tell four funny jokes

00:13:28.707 --> 00:13:30.208
about a national day
of the week.

00:13:30.208 --> 00:13:31.543
For those who don't know,
this is our friend

00:13:31.543 --> 00:13:33.111
Mike Scollins right here.
Let's just show him off.

00:13:33.111 --> 00:13:34.179
There you go.

00:13:34.179 --> 00:13:36.715
[ Laughter ]

00:13:36.715 --> 00:13:38.484
That's Mike
in his everyday outfit.

00:13:38.484 --> 00:13:40.252
[ Laughter ]

00:13:40.252 --> 00:13:44.056
And, now, we're gonna find out
if he can "tank-top" himself.

00:13:44.056 --> 00:13:48.560
[ Laughter ]

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:51.063
And, finally,
today was Pecan Day.

00:13:51.063 --> 00:13:53.232
Well, I hope you got a nut.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:56.935
Judges?

00:13:56.935 --> 00:14:01.439
[ Laughter ]

00:14:01.439 --> 00:14:02.908
Ahh!

00:14:02.908 --> 00:14:05.110
[ Laughter ]

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:06.211
Heartbreaking.

00:14:06.211 --> 00:14:09.214
[ Laughter ]

00:14:09.214 --> 00:14:10.749
That was the monologue,
everybody.

00:14:10.749 --> 00:14:14.219 line:0%
♪♪

00:14:14.219 --> 00:14:16.021 line:0%
[ Whistling and applause ]

